  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday Night through Thursday)\nIssued at 1045 PM CST Thu Nov 5 2026\n\nMid level ridging will dominate through the weekend while a\nCanadian surface high settles over the area Friday night through\nSunday. Clearing skies will allow for a couple of chilly Fall\nnights across the region, with temperatures likely dropping into\nthe 30s both Saturday and Sunday morning across the north. Areas\nof frost or a possible light freeze will be possible for some\nof the normally colder locations, especially by Sunday morning.\nDry conditions persist through the weekend under the influence of\nhigh pressure.\n\nThe surface high will gradually shift east by early next week, \nallowing southerly surface winds to return to the region. This \nwill kick off a warming trend through mid week as temperatures \nrebound back above normal. Mostly dry conditions are forecast \nthrough the end of the period. A slow moving cutoff mid level low \nwill meander across south Texas late this weekend. Guidance \ndiverges on the evolution of this wave by early next week. Some \nindications are that it could lift northeast across southern \nOklahoma sometime early to mid next week, which could bring some \nscattered showers to the area along with more cloud cover and \ncooler highs than currently forecast. Otherwise, pleasant \nconditions will be the rule through much of the next week.\n\nBowlan",
